		summary = "A **village** is a [[Human settlement|human settlement]] or a residential community, larger than a hamlet but smaller than a [[Town|town]]; some geographers describe villages as having between 500 and 2,500 inhabitants. Although villages are often located in [[Rural area|rural areas]], the term urban village is also applied to certain urban neighborhoods. Villages are normally permanent, with fixed dwellings, however, transient villages also exist. Further, the dwellings of a village are fairly close to one another, not scattered broadly over the landscape, as a dispersed settlement. In the past, villages were a usual form of community for societies that practiced [[Subsistence agriculture|subsistence agriculture]] and also for some non-agricultural societies.",
		sections = {
